/**
 * Memory-on / Memory-off twin capture harness (issue #126, SPEC #107 AC 35–37).
 *
 * The Memory-off comparison arm is generated by explicit non-authoritative
 * Replay over the same frozen input, never by production shadowing
 * (ADR-0071 / ADR-0073): both arms run the highest authenticated Text system
 * seam — the production BFF NDJSON handler over the real Conversation
 * ResponseService, Agent Harness, Action Gateway, Context Compiler, and
 * Provider Egress adapter — against a disposable isolated PostgreSQL schema
 * that is dropped after the run. No product state is ever written.
 *
 * The two arms differ only in the production write switches:
 *
 * - Memory-on  — the cutover configuration: fast-path extraction enqueued and
 *   dispatched through the real outbox machinery, due consolidation scans
 *   queued and dispatched at day boundaries, and the Structured-Lexical
 *   retrieval baseline wired into the Context Compiler (#116/#117).
 * - Memory-off — the same seam with the memory write switches off
 *   (`SAYHEAR_FAST_PATH_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=false` /
 *   `SAYHEAR_MEMORY_CONSOLIDATION_ENABLED=false` /
 *   `SAYHEAR_MEMORY_RETRIEVAL_ENABLED=false` in production terms): no claims
 *   are written, no memory sections compile, and the arm behaves as the
 *   pre-memory incumbent under the same persona and champion.
 *
 * The role registry (memory.extract / entity.resolve / memory.consolidate and
 * the conversation champion) is injectable so the system test can script the
 * memory roles deterministically while the evidence run uses the real
 * responses-api registry.
 */
